<Base lang="en" title="Caldrew | Team" description="The people behind Caldrew. Operators who have run, turned around and sold companies themselves.">
<section class="cd-page-header"><div class="cd-container"><p class="cd-eyebrow">Team</p><h1 class="cd-page-title">Operators who have sat on your side of the table.</h1></div></section><section class="cd-numbered"><div class="cd-container"><div class="cd-team-grid"><div><img src="/images/dcg.jpeg" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 33vw" srcset="/images/dcg-p-500.jpeg 500w, /images/dcg-p-800.jpeg 800w, /images/dcg-p-1080.jpeg 1080w, /images/dcg.jpeg 1125w" alt="" class="cd-portrait"/><h2 class="cd-member-name">Duarte Gonçalves</h2><p class="cd-member-role">Investment Analyst</p><p class="cd-member-bio">Duarte supports Caldrew&#x27;s investment work: sourcing, valuation, modelling and the analysis behind each deal. He came up in M&amp;A and transaction advisory, earlier at Beresford Capital and Haitong, and holds a Master&#x27;s in Finance from Católica Lisbon.</p></div><div><img src="/images/hmc.jpeg" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 33vw" srcset="/images/hmc-p-500.jpeg 500w, /images/hmc-p-800.jpeg 800w, /images/hmc-p-1080.jpeg 1080w, /images/hmc.jpeg 1125w" alt="" class="cd-portrait"/><h2 class="cd-member-name">Hugo Martins da Costa</h2><p class="cd-member-role">Chief Financial Officer</p><p class="cd-member-bio">Hugo leads Caldrew&#x27;s finance function: the reporting, structure and governance that long-term ownership depends on. He held director roles at Banco BIG and Banco Finantia, and taught as an assistant professor, bringing the discipline of someone who has worked deals from the numbers up.</p></div><div><img src="/images/jb.jpeg" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 33vw" srcset="/images/jb-p-500.jpeg 500w, /images/jb-p-800.jpeg 800w, /images/jb-p-1080.jpeg 1080w, /images/jb.jpeg 1122w" alt="" class="cd-portrait"/><h2 class="cd-member-name">João Bento</h2><p class="cd-member-role">Non-Executive Partner</p><p class="cd-member-bio">Former CEO of CTT, where he led the company&#x27;s transformation from Portugal&#x27;s postal operator into a leading Iberian logistics group. Earlier he ran Efacec and Grupo Manuel Champalimaud, and was COO of Brisa. As Non-Executive Partner, he brings the judgement of a career spent leading companies at scale.</p></div><div><img src="/images/jsa.jpeg" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 33vw" srcset="/images/jsa-p-500.jpeg 500w, /images/jsa-p-800.jpeg 800w, /images/jsa-p-1080.jpeg 1080w, /images/jsa.jpeg 1126w" alt="" class="cd-portrait"/><h2 class="cd-member-name">João de Sousa Aroso</h2><p class="cd-member-role">Founding Partner</p><p class="cd-member-bio">Founded Leadzai and led it as CEO through its sale. Earlier, he led the acquisition, turnaround and sale of Páginas Amarelas, the kind of work Caldrew now does as a firm. He also serves on the board of Erakulis.</p></div><div><img src="/images/mqp.jpeg" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 33vw" srcset="/images/mqp-p-500.jpeg 500w, /images/mqp-p-800.jpeg 800w, /images/mqp-p-1080.jpeg 1080w, /images/mqp.jpeg 1125w" alt="" class="cd-portrait"/><h2 class="cd-member-name">Manuel Queiroz Pereira</h2><p class="cd-member-role">Founding Partner</p><p class="cd-member-bio">A family office principal with 20 years of investment experience across sectors in Portugal. As co-founder of Caldrew, he brings an owner&#x27;s perspective, shaped by investing his own capital, with a focus on disciplined capital allocation and long-term value creation.</p></div><div><img src="/images/mmv.jpeg" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 33vw" srcset="/images/mmv-p-500.jpeg 500w, /images/mmv-p-800.jpeg 800w, /images/mmv-p-1080.jpeg 1080w, /images/mmv.jpeg 1126w" alt="" class="cd-portrait"/><h2 class="cd-member-name">Miguel Mora do Vale</h2><p class="cd-member-role">Advisory Board Member</p><p class="cd-member-bio">A Law graduate, Miguel Mora do Vale is a lawyer and board member of several companies, combining legal and business expertise across different sectors. As a member of Caldrew&#x27;s Advisory Board, he will contribute his strategic and independent perspective to investment assessment, legal matters, risk mitigation and the strengthening of corporate governance practices, supporting informed decision-making, business sustainability and long-term value creation.</p></div></div></div></section>
</Base>
